    "quality/rfc-compliance/profiles/edge/index.html": "\u003c!doctype html\u003e\n\u003chtml lang=\"en\"\u003e\n    \u003chead\u003e\n        \u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" /\u003e\n        \u003cscript id=\"theme-bootstrap\"\u003e(function(){var t=\"light\";try{var s=localStorage.getItem(\"ze-theme\");t=s===\"dark\"||s===\"light\"?s:window.matchMedia\u0026\u0026window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\").matches?\"dark\":\"light\"}catch(e){t=window.matchMedia\u0026\u0026window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\").matches?\"dark\":\"light\"}document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\",t)})();\u003c/script\u003e\n        \u003ctitle\u003eEdge RFC coverage - Ze\u003c/title\u003e\n        \u003cmeta name=\"description\" content=\"Release profile edge: the MUST and overview coverage of its RFCs.\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Edge RFC coverage - Ze\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Release profile edge: the MUST and overview coverage of its RFCs.\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://ze-software.net/assets/social-card.png\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"630\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:image:alt\" content=\"Ze, an open-source configuration and protocol engine\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Edge RFC coverage - Ze\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Release profile edge: the MUST and overview coverage of its RFCs.\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://ze-software.net/assets/social-card.png\" /\u003e\n        \u003clink rel=\"icon\" href=\"../../../../assets/ze.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" /\u003e\n        \u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../../assets/vendor/fonts/fonts.css\" /\u003e\n        \u003clink rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://ze-software.net/quality/rfc-compliance/profiles/edge/\" /\u003e\n        \u003cmeta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://ze-software.net/quality/rfc-compliance/profiles/edge/\" /\u003e\n        \u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../../assets/site.css\" /\u003e\n        \u003cscript type=\"application/ld+json\"\u003e{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"Ze\",\"url\":\"https://ze-software.net/\",\"description\":\"Open-source configuration and protocol engine for Linux routing, with YANG-modeled plugins, operator interfaces, telemetry, and MCP.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"},{\"@type\":\"SoftwareSourceCode\",\"name\":\"Ze\",\"description\":\"Open-source configuration and protocol engine for Linux routing, used to build a plugin-based network operating system.\",\"codeRepository\":\"https://github.com/ze-software/ze\",\"license\":\"https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.en.html\",\"programmingLanguage\":\"Go\",\"runtimePlatform\":\"Linux\",\"applicationCategory\":\"Network operating system\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":true}]}\u003c/script\u003e\n    \u003c/head\u003e\n    \u003cbody\u003e\n        \u003ca class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#top\"\u003eSkip to main content\u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003cdiv id=\"site-header-mount\" data-header-src=\"../../../../assets/header.html\" data-site-root=\"../../../../\"\u003e\n            \u003cnoscript\u003e\n                \u003cnav class=\"site-header-fallback\" aria-label=\"Site navigation\"\u003e\n                    \u003ca class=\"brand\" href=\"../../../../#top\"\u003eZe\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../#top\"\u003eHome\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../docs/\"\u003eDocs\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../features/\"\u003eFeatures\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../compare/\"\u003eCompare\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../project/roadmap/\"\u003eRoadmap\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../project/changes/\"\u003eChanges\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../faq/\"\u003eFAQ\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../contribute/\"\u003eContribute\u003c/a\u003e\n                \u003c/nav\u003e\n            \u003c/noscript\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cmain id=\"top\" tabindex=\"-1\"\u003e\n            \u003csection aria-labeledby=\"rfc-profile-title\" class=\"md-content reveal cat-observe\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"journey-hero reveal\"\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"journey-eyebrow\"\u003eRelease profile\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003ch1 id=\"rfc-profile-title\"\u003eEdge\u003c/h1\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThe RFCs this use case requires, each declared by the Use cases row of its own summary. RFCs it lists as optional follow in their own table and never enter its figures. Before release, every mandatory requirement of every required RFC must be proven by a recorded break of its test.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cstyle\u003e\n.rfc-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }\n.rfc-id-list { margin: .6rem 0; line-height: 1.9; }\n.rfc-verdict { margin: 1rem 0 1.6rem; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 18px; background: var(--panel-strong); border: 1px solid var(--line); box-shadow: 0 1rem 2rem -1.6rem var(--shadow); }\n.rfc-verdict p { margin: 0 0 .4rem; color: var(--muted); }\n.rfc-verdict p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }\n.rfc-verdict span { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n.rfc-verdict strong { display: block; margin: .2rem 0 .5rem; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); line-height: 1; color: var(--text); }\n.rfc-card-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(13rem, 1fr)); grid-auto-rows: 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 .8rem; }\n.rfc-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-radius: 18px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: var(--panel-strong); border: 1px solid var(--line); box-shadow: 0 1rem 2rem -1.6rem var(--shadow); }\n.rfc-card span { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n.rfc-card strong { display: block; margin: .3rem 0 .15rem; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.55rem); line-height: 1; color: var(--text); }\n.rfc-card b { display: block; margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: var(--text); font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 700; }\n.rfc-card p { margin: auto 0 0; padding-top: .35rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; }\n.rfc-ok { border-left: 7px solid var(--green); }\n.rfc-neutral { border-left: 7px solid var(--line-strong); }\n.rfc-warn { border-left: 7px solid var(--amber); }\n.rfc-bad { border-left: 7px solid var(--danger-deep); }\n.rfc-tape { display: flex; height: 1.5rem; margin: 1rem 0 .8rem; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); background: var(--panel); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.75); }\n.rfc-tape span { width: var(--w); min-width: 0; display: block; }\n.rfc-tape-key { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .35rem 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 1.4rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; font-size: .92rem; }\n.rfc-tape-key li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .45rem; }\n.rfc-swatch { display: inline-block; width: .85rem; height: .85rem; border-radius: .25rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); vertical-align: -.1rem; }\n.rfc-tape-both_polarities { background: var(--teal-chip); }\n.rfc-tape-single_polarity { background: var(--sky-chip); }\n.rfc-tape-not_applicable { background: var(--grape-chip); }\n.rfc-tape-feature_declined { background: var(--pink-chip); }\n.rfc-tape-lower_layer { background: var(--mint-chip); }\n.rfc-tape-linux_limit { background: var(--muted); }\n.rfc-tape-rollup { background: var(--tangerine-chip); }\n.rfc-tape-gap { background: var(--gold-chip); }\n.rfc-tape-partial-scope { background: var(--danger-deep); }\n.rfc-tape-one_polarity_unexcused { background: var(--amber); }\n.rfc-tape-missing_unexcused { background: var(--danger-deep); }\n.rfc-swatch.rfc-ok { background: var(--green); }\n.rfc-swatch.rfc-neutral { background: var(--line-strong); }\n.rfc-swatch.rfc-warn { background: var(--amber); }\n.rfc-swatch.rfc-bad { background: var(--danger-deep); }\n.rfc-total td { border-top: 2px solid var(--line-strong); }\n.rfc-prose { max-width: 46rem; }\nul.rfc-prose { margin: .5rem 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }\nul.rfc-prose li { margin: .35rem 0; line-height: 1.6; }\np.rfc-prose { margin: .5rem 0; line-height: 1.6; }\n.rfc-fold { margin: .6rem 0; }\n.rfc-fold \u003e summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; }\n.rfc-span \u003e td { padding-bottom: .2rem; border-bottom: 0; }\n.rfc-table td:first-child { font-weight: 400; }\n.rfc-table .rfc-span \u003e td { padding-top: .9rem; }\n.rfc-subject-id { white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; }\n.rfc-subject { display: block; max-width: 52rem; }\n.rfc-tests { display: grid; gap: .15rem .8rem; }\n.rfc-tests-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5rem 9.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .8rem; align-items: baseline; }\n.rfc-tests-row \u003e span:first-child { color: var(--muted); font-size: .88rem; }\n.rfc-mark { margin: .45rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); max-width: 52rem; }\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\n  .rfc-tests-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; padding-bottom: .35rem; }\n}\n.rfc-text \u003e summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }\n.rfc-text \u003e p { margin: .35rem 0 0; max-width: 44rem; }\n.rfc-note-box { margin: 1rem 0; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 16px; background: var(--gold-tint); border: 1px solid var(--gold-chip); }\n.rfc-note-box h3 { margin-top: 0; }\n.rfc-note-box ul { margin-bottom: 0; }\n.rfc-check-ok strong { color: var(--green); }\n.rfc-check-bad strong { color: var(--danger-deep); }\n\u003c/style\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"../\"\u003eAll profiles\u003c/a\u003e · \u003ca href=\"../../\"\u003eAll RFCs\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003csection\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFigures\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMUST bar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"profile/edge/required:must\"\u003eZe proven 7, OS verified 2, OS testing gap 1, Ze correctness gap 1,200\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOverview bar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"profile/edge/required:overview\"\u003eZe MUST proven 7, OS verified 3, SHOULD proven 1, Not owed 12, SHOULD not ever 1, SHOULD not yet 2, SHOULD not decided 2, OS testing gap 2, Ze correctness gap 1,200\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"rfc-table-wrap\"\u003e\n\u003ctable class=\"rfc-table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eFigure\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eRows\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eRFCs\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:rfcs\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eNot walked\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:not-walked\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMandatory register\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:register\"\u003enot complete\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST rows\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.total\"\u003e1,220\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST rows kept (the MUST bar)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.kept\"\u003e1,210\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eZe proven\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.ze-proven\"\u003e7\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOS verified\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.os-verified\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOS testing gap\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.os-gap\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eZe correctness gap\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.ze-gap\"\u003e1,200\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST rows not owed\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.not-owed\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST not owed: feature-declined\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.not-owed-by-kind.feature-declined\"\u003e6\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST not owed: linux-limit\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.not-owed-by-kind.linux-limit\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST not owed: not-applicable\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:must.not-owed-by-kind.not-applicable\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD / MAY rows\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.total\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD proven\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.proven\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD OS verified\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.os-verified\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD OS testing gap\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.os-gap\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.not-owed\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed: feature-declined\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.not-owed-by-kind.feature-declined\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed: linux-limit\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.not-owed-by-kind.linux-limit\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed: not-applicable\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.not-owed-by-kind.not-applicable\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not ever\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.not-ever\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not yet\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.not-yet\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not decided\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/required:should.not-decided\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe MUST bar counts the MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL and SHALL NOT rows of the walked RFCs that the stack owes: Ze proven means a recorded test break proves the row; a row a layer under Ze performs is OS verified when a test checks that layer on the state Ze installs, an OS testing gap until one does. The overview bar adds the MAY, NOT RECOMMENDED, OPTIONAL, RECOMMENDED, SHOULD and SHOULD NOT rows and the rows not owed, which do not bind Ze. An RFC that is not walked has no valid extraction sign-off, so its rows count in no figure. Every count is read from the RFC data files when the page loads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/section\u003e\n\u003csection\u003e\u003ch2\u003eTree\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoots first: an RFC sits one level above the highest level of the RFCs it builds on, and the RFCs of one citation cycle share a level. Each RFC carries the same two bars as the set above, from its own data file; an RFC that is not walked shows \u0026#34;not walked\u0026#34; and no bar. The last column names the summary whose Use cases row declares the RFC: a normative citation never adds one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eLevel 0\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"rfc-table-wrap\"\u003e\n\u003ctable class=\"rfc-table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eRFC\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eTitle\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eMUST bar\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eOverview bar\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eWhy it is here\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"../../rfc1/\"\u003eRFC 1\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRFC rfc1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc1:must\"\u003eZe proven 3, OS verified 2, OS testing gap 1, Ze correctness gap 1,200\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc1:overview\"\u003eZe MUST proven 3, OS verified 3, SHOULD proven 1, Not owed 12, SHOULD not ever 1, SHOULD not yet 2, SHOULD not decided 2, OS testing gap 2, Ze correctness gap 1,200\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eedge: required by rfc/short/rfc1.md\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"../../rfc2/\"\u003eRFC 2\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRFC rfc2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc2:must\"\u003eZe proven 4\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc2:overview\"\u003eZe MUST proven 4\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eedge: required by rfc/short/rfc2.md\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eLevel 1\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"rfc-table-wrap\"\u003e\n\u003ctable class=\"rfc-table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eRFC\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eTitle\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eMUST bar\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eOverview bar\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eWhy it is here\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"../../rfc3/\"\u003eRFC 3\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRFC rfc3\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc3:must\"\u003enot walked\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc3:overview\"\u003enot walked\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eedge: required by rfc/short/rfc3.md\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/section\u003e\n\u003csection\u003e\u003ch2\u003eOptional (not counted)\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRFCs this use case lists as optional, each declared by the Optional use cases row of its own summary. They count in none of the figures above until the owner brings one into scope by moving it to the Use cases row. Their own bars and figures follow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMUST bar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"profile/edge/optional:must\"\u003eZe proven 9\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOverview bar\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"profile/edge/optional:overview\"\u003eZe MUST proven 9\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"rfc-table-wrap\"\u003e\n\u003ctable class=\"rfc-table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eFigure\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eRows\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eRFCs\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:rfcs\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eNot walked\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:not-walked\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMandatory register\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:register\"\u003ecomplete\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST rows\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.total\"\u003e9\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST rows kept (the MUST bar)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.kept\"\u003e9\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eZe proven\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.ze-proven\"\u003e9\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOS verified\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.os-verified\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOS testing gap\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.os-gap\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eZe correctness gap\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.ze-gap\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST rows not owed\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.not-owed\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST not owed: feature-declined\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.not-owed-by-kind.feature-declined\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST not owed: linux-limit\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.not-owed-by-kind.linux-limit\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMUST not owed: not-applicable\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:must.not-owed-by-kind.not-applicable\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD / MAY rows\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.total\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD proven\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.proven\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD OS verified\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.os-verified\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD OS testing gap\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.os-gap\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.not-owed\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed: feature-declined\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.not-owed-by-kind.feature-declined\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed: linux-limit\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.not-owed-by-kind.linux-limit\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not owed: not-applicable\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.not-owed-by-kind.not-applicable\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not ever\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.not-ever\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not yet\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.not-yet\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSHOULD not decided\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cspan data-ze-rfc=\"profile/edge/optional:should.not-decided\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe MUST bar counts the MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL and SHALL NOT rows of the walked RFCs that the stack owes: Ze proven means a recorded test break proves the row; a row a layer under Ze performs is OS verified when a test checks that layer on the state Ze installs, an OS testing gap until one does. The overview bar adds the MAY, NOT RECOMMENDED, OPTIONAL, RECOMMENDED, SHOULD and SHOULD NOT rows and the rows not owed, which do not bind Ze. An RFC that is not walked has no valid extraction sign-off, so its rows count in no figure. Every count is read from the RFC data files when the page loads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"rfc-table-wrap\"\u003e\n\u003ctable class=\"rfc-table\"\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eRFC\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eTitle\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eMUST bar\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eOverview bar\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eWhy it is here\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"../../rfc4/\"\u003eRFC 4\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRFC rfc4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc4:must\"\u003eZe proven 9\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cdiv data-ze-rfc-bar=\"rfc4:overview\"\u003eZe MUST proven 9\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eedge: optional in rfc/short/rfc4.md\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/section\u003e\n\u003cscript src=\"../../../../assets/rfc-figures.js\" defer\u003e\u003c/script\u003e\n            \u003c/section\u003e\n        \u003c/main\u003e\n\n        \u003cscript src=\"../../../../assets/site.js\" defer\u003e\u003c/script\u003e\n\n        \u003cfooter\u003e\n            \u003cdiv class=\"footer-inner\"\u003e\n                \u003cdiv class=\"footer-bottom\"\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"footer-copyright\"\u003e© 2025-2026 Thomas Mangin.\u003c/span\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../license/\"\u003eZe is AGPLv3 open source.\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003ca href=\"../../../../legal/\"\u003eLegal notice\u003c/a\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"footer-published\"\u003ePublished 31 October 2026 12:00 UTC\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003c/div\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/footer\u003e\n    \u003c/body\u003e\n\u003c/html\u003e\n"
